      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ أَتَقَبَّلُ اَلثِّيَابَ أَخِيطُهَا فَأُعْطِيهَا اَلْغِلْمَانَ بِالثُّلُثَيْنِ قَالَ \"أَ لَيْسَ تَعْمَلُ فِيهَا\" قُلْتُ أُقَطِّعُهَا وَ أَشْتَرِي لَهُمُ اَلْخُيُوطَ قَالَ \"لاَ بَأْسَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3912 - Safwan bin Yahya narrated from Abu Muhammad Al-Khayyat, from Mujammi', who said: I said to Abu Abdillah (as),\n\"I take on garments to sew and then give them to young workers, keeping one-third and giving them two-thirds. Is this permissible?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Don't you also work on them?\"\nI said: \"I cut the fabric and buy the threads for them.\"\nImam (as) said: \"There is no harm in that.\""
        ]
      }
    },
